@startuml
' Phase 4 — Sifter: planned infrastructure. Authored at phase start.
' Copy to summary.uml at phase end and edit to the as-built state.

title Phase 4 — Sifter (planned)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "aa-sifter (Python, src/aa_sifter)" as sifter {
  component "app (ComputeSifter orchestration)" as app
  component "contracts (aa_contracts bridge)" as bridge
  component "rpc (JSON-RPC 2.0 service)" as rpc
  component "decisions (classify + approval + rules)" as decisions
  component "routing (preflight + policy + budget)" as routing
  component "context (handoff + redaction + sizing)" as context
  component "models (providers + config)" as models
  component "catalog + recommend + system" as recommend
  component "tasks (DAG + executor)" as tasks
  component "verification" as verify
  component "metrics (usage + trace)" as metrics
  component "memory (MemorySink)" as memory
  component "history (SQLite)" as history
  component "cli + desktop" as surfaces
}

package "aa-contracts (Python bindings)" as contracts

contracts --> bridge : route / memory schemas

rpc --> bridge
rpc --> app
app --> decisions
app --> routing
app --> context
app --> models
app --> tasks
app --> verify
app --> metrics
app --> memory
app --> history
surfaces --> app
recommend --> models

note right of context
  ADR-P4-003: every expert-tier
  outbound request passes through
  the single redaction chokepoint.
end note

note bottom of routing
  ADR-P4-004/005: token limits and
  budget are enforced; cost waivers
  and standing-rule grants are wired.
end note

note bottom of rpc
  sifter.route -> route_response
  sifter.generate -> {text, usage}
  sifter.health -> {available, providers[]}
end note

note bottom of memory
  ADR-P4-008: traces emitted as
  memory_record candidates; no
  canonical state is written here.
end note

@enduml
